.TH true "" "Command"
.SH NAME
true \- unconditional success
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrue\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
true -- unconditional success
Usage:	true
Does nothing and returns exit status 0.
.HE
.B true
does nothing and exits with a zero (success) status.
It is useful in shell scripts as the always-satisfied condition of a loop, as in
.DS
.ta 8n
	\fBwhile true; do ... done\fR
.DE
which repeats its body until broken out of explicitly.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B true
always exits with status 0.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sh ,
.B false
